    "reading": {
        "body": "The tracked model count stands at 16,355 as of September 24, 2026, but the daily series shows two abrupt downward revisions in August, so the headline total reflects a redefined dataset rather than continuous accumulation.\n\nMonthly additions show a clear acceleration. From October 2024 through early 2025, new models per month ranged from 248 to 422. By spring 2026 that rose to 741 in April and 817 in May, then jumped to 1,362 in August 2026. September 2026 already has 1,106 new models through the 24th, putting it on pace to exceed August.\n\nThe newest releases span music, financial, vision, image generation, and robotics models, so the acceleration is broad rather than confined to one modality. The data does not record model size, training compute, or the organizations behind each release, so it cannot directly measure the power or hardware demand this cadence creates.",
